Tracker</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cbinsights.com/research-vc-glossary-index/">VC Glossary</a></li><li><a href="https://www.cbinsights.com/research-company-list-applications">Company List Applications</a></li></ul></section></nav></div><div class="Footer-module__Grjkva__footer-separator"></div><ul class="Footer-module__Grjkva__footer-moreInfoLinks"><li class="Footer-module__Grjkva__footer-moreInfoLink"><a href="https://www.cbinsights.com/website-terms-of-use/" class="text-inherit">CB Insights Website Terms of Use</a></li><li class="Footer-module__Grjkva__footer-moreInfoLink"><a href="https://www.cbinsights.com/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a></li><li class="Footer-module__Grjkva__footer-moreInfoLink"><a href="https://preferences.cbinsights.com/dont_sell" class="text-inherit">Do Not Sell My Info</a></li><li class="Footer-module__Grjkva__footer-moreInfoLink"><a href="https://www.cbinsights.com/research-partnerships">Partnership</a></li></ul><p class="Footer-module__Grjkva__footer-copyright">Copyright <!-- -->2026<!-- --> CB Information Services, Inc. All rights reserved.</p></div></footer><div data-test="cookie-banner" class="CookieBanner-module__vZF3uG__cookieBanner"><div data-test="cookie-banner-content" class="CookieBanner-module__vZF3uG__cookieContent"><div class="fontSize--s padding--y--m align--center"><p><span>CBI websites generally use certain cookies to enable better interactions with </span><span>our sites and services. Use of these cookies, which may be stored on your device, </span><span>permits us to improve and customize your experience. You can read more about your </span><span>cookie choices at <a href="https://www.cbinsights.com/privacy-policy">our privacy policy</a>. By continuing to use this</span><span> site you are consenting to these choices.</span></p></div><div class="CookieBanner-module__vZF3uG__buttonsContainer"><div class="CookieBanner-module__vZF3uG__buttonContainer"><button class="py-0 px-[15px] font-medium text-m leading-[normal] select-none rounded-sm !inline-flex justify-center items-center focus:outline-0 focus:shadow-focus transition-all duration-250 text-white border border-solid border-transparent bg-blue hover:bg-blue-600 active:bg-blue-500"><div class="relative inline-flex"><span class="py-[7px]">I ACCEPT</span></div></button></div><div class="CookieBanner-module__vZF3uG__buttonContainer"><button class="py-0 px-[15px] font-medium text-m leading-[normal] select-none rounded-sm !inline-flex justify-center items-center focus:outline-0 focus:shadow-focus transition-all duration-250 border border-solid border-transparent text-charcoal hover:bg-charcoal/12 active:bg-charcoal/24"><div class="relative inline-flex"><span class="py-[7px]">I DO NOT ACCEPT</span></div></button></div></div></div></div></main></div><script id="__NEXT_DATA__" type="application/json" crossorigin="anonymous">{"props":{"pageProps":{"data":{"profile_json":{"1":{"news":[{"date":"2026-07-08","title":"Pune founder 'extremely concerned' with flooding in peak sale season: 'Warehouses suffered...'","content":"Ganesh Sonawane, founder and CEO of wellness brand Frido, has said he is \"extremely concerned\" about the ongoing rain situation in Maharashtra after one of the company's major warehouses reportedly suffered significant damage in a landslide amid the peak e-commerce sale season. In a post on X, Sonawane said persistent rain had created operational challenges for the company, with roads outside warehouses submerged and logistics networks coming under strain. \"Extremely concerned about the rain situation amidst the peak e-commerce sale season. Roads outside warehouses are waterlogged, and one of our major warehouses suffered significant damage due to a landslide last night,\" he wrote. \"Please note that there may be delays in shipments. We sincerely apologize for the inconvenience and appreciate your understanding.\" Responding to a user in the comments, Sonawane said the damaged warehouse was located near Talegaon, close to the highway. He also shared a video of the flooded highway. The 32-second video received over a million views. Extremely concerned about the rain situation amidst the peak e-commerce sale season. Roads outside warehouses are waterlogged, and one of our major warehouses suffered significant damage due to a landslide last night. Praying for everyone’s safety. Please note that there may… pic.twitter.com/tuXfcbQSNs — Ganesh Sonawane (@ganeshsonawane) July 6, 2026 Rain hits businesses during key sales period The post comes as Maharashtra grapples with intense monsoon activity that has disrupted transport and logistics across several regions. For e-commerce and consumer-facing businesses, the timing is particularly challenging as the ongoing sale season typically sees a surge in order volumes. Waterlogged roads, damaged infrastructure and transportation disruptions can affect inventory movement, last-mile delivery operations and warehouse functioning. While Sonawane did not disclose the extent of the losses, he indicated that customers could face shipment delays as the company deals with the fallout from the weather event. Social media reacts The post attracted comments from users who said such disruptions have become a recurring problem during every monsoon. One user wrote that businesses face similar issues each rainy season despite significant spending on infrastructure projects. \"Every rainy season we face this problem. Millions are spent on solutions each year, yet the situation only worsens and there's no accountability for how the money is used.\" Another user expressed frustration over the impact of heavy taxation and business risks, while pointing to flooding and poor infrastructure. A separate comment highlighted concerns about the safety of commercial vehicle drivers who continue operating during extreme weather conditions. Maharashtra rains trigger landslides, transport disruptions Sonawane's account emerged against the backdrop of severe rainfall across the Mumbai-Pune region that has already disrupted rail and air connectivity. According to Moneycontrol, a landslide in the South East Ghat section between Karjat and Lonavala led to the cancellation of 16 trains and diversion of nine others on the busy Mumbai-Pune corridor. The disruption followed continuous heavy rainfall in the ghat section. The India Meteorological Department had issued a red alert for Pune, while heavy rains also affected Mumbai and surrounding regions. Flight operations were impacted as well, with cancellations and diversions reported due to adverse weather. A separate report noted that the Karjat-Lonavala ghat section received exceptionally heavy rainfall, with Lonavala recording about 670 mm of rain in a 24-hour period. Officials said multiple landslides were reported across the region, while Pune district witnessed landslides at 22 locations over two days. The rainfall caused widespread disruption to railway operations, with dozens of train services cancelled, diverted or rescheduled as restoration teams worked to clear debris and repair damaged sections of track.","url":"https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/trends/pune-founder-extremely-concerned-with-flooding-in-peak-sale-season-warehouses-suffered-13968827.html"},{"date":"2026-06-29","title":"Frido partners HYROX India for Delhi, Mumbai events","content":"afaqs! news bureau  Ergonomics and comfort solutions brand Frido has partnered with HYROX India for its upcoming fitness racing events in Delhi and Mumbai.  Under the partnership, Frido will be the Official Knee Cap Partner for Masters' Union HYROX Delhi, scheduled from 24 to 26 July, and the Official Nasal Strip Partner for Masters' Union HYROX Mumbai, which will take place from 17 to 20 September.  During these events, Frido will showcase its Orthotics Sports Knee Cap Support and Nasal Strip Pro products, designed to support joint stability and improve breathing during high intensity physical activity.  Ganesh Sonawane, co-founder and CEO, Frido, said, \"There is a growing focus on movement quality, recovery and long-term physical health, alongside performance. HYROX has cultivated a community that reflects this shift, making it a natural platform for us to engage with.\"  Deepak Raj, country head, HYROX India, said, \"India is fast becoming one of the most exciting markets for HYROX, with a rapidly growing community of athletes eager to test themselves against a single global standard. We are delighted to welcome Frido as our Knee Cap Partner in Delhi and Nasal Strip Partner in Mumbai, giving participants hands-on access to products built around movement and comfort as they take on the challenge.\"","url":"https://www.afaqs.com/news/mktg/frido-partners-hyrox-india-for-delhi-mumbai-events-12116732"},{"date":"2026-06-29","title":"Frido Joins Masters’ Union HYROX Delhi and Mumbai as an Official Partner","content":"India, June 29: Frido, India’s leading D2C ergonomics and comfort solutions brand, has announced its partnership with HYROX India for its upcoming fitness racing events in Delhi and Mumbai. As part of the association, Frido will be the Official Knee Cap Partner for Masters’ Union HYROX Delhi, scheduled from July 24 to 26, 2026, and the Official Nasal Strip Partner for Masters’ Union HYROX Mumbai, scheduled from September 17 to 20, 2026. HYROX has emerged as one of the world’s fastest-growing fitness race formats, pairing eight 1-kilometre runs with eight functional workout stations in a standardised global format that test endurance, strength, speed and consistency. As the format gains momentum in India, Frido’s collaboration with HYROX India’s upcoming races in Delhi and Mumbai reflects the brand’s growing focus on performance-led wellness and movement-enhancing solutions. For athletes taking on a competition that tests endurance, strength and consistency, factors such as joint stability and efficient breathing can play an important role in overall performance. Reflecting these needs, Frido will showcase two products from its portfolio: Frido Orthotics Sports Knee Cap Support and Frido Nasal Strip Pro. The Knee Cap Support is designed to provide targeted compression and stability during high-impact movement, while the Nasal Strip Pro helps optimize airflow and breathing efficiency during intense physical exertion. Together, these solutions are designed to help participants train, compete and recover with greater confidence and comfort. Speaking on the association, Ganesh Sonawane, Co-Founder and CEO, Frido, said, “The way consumers approach fitness and wellbeing is evolving rapidly. There is a growing focus on movement quality, recovery and long-term physical health, alongside performance. HYROX has cultivated a community that reflects this shift, making it a natural platform for us to engage with. This partnership aligns with our vision of creating products that help people move more comfortably and confidently, whether they are preparing for competition or navigating everyday life.”\nDeepak Raj, Country Head, HYROX India, said, “India is fast becoming one of the most exciting markets for HYROX, with a rapidly growing community of athletes eager to test themselves against a single global standard. We are delighted to welcome Frido as our Knee Cap Partner in Delhi and Nasal Strip Partner in Mumbai, giving participants hands-on access to products built around movement and comfort as they take on the challenge. Partners who share our commitment to performance and wellbeing make the HYROX experience stronger, and we look forward to building this journey together.”\nThe initiative enables Frido to connect with India’s growing community of runners, athletes and fitness enthusiasts while driving greater awareness around the role of movement, recovery and performance-focused solutions in an active lifestyle. Across both events, the brand will engage with participants and spectators, offering firsthand experiences of products designed to enhance endurance, comfort and overall physical performance.","url":"https://businessnewsthisweek.com/business/frido-joins-masters-union-hyrox-delhi-and-mumbai-as-an-official-partner/"},{"date":"2026-06-29","title":"Frido Joins Masters' Union HYROX Delhi and Mumbai as an Official Partner","content":"fitness racing events in Delhi and Mumbai . As part of the association, Frido will be the Official Knee Cap Partner for Masters Union HYROX Delhi , scheduled from July 24 to 26, 2026, and the Official Nasal Strip Partner for Masters Union HYROX Mumbai , scheduled from September 17 to 20, 2026.  HYROX has emerged as one of the world's fastest-growing fitness race formats, pairing eight 1-kilometre runs with eight functional workout stations in a standardised global format that test endurance, strength, speed and consistency. As the format gains momentum in India, Frido 's collaboration with HYROX India's upcoming races in Delhi and Mumbai reflects the brand's growing focus on performance-led wellness and movement-enhancing solutions.  For athletes taking on a competition that tests endurance, strength and consistency, factors such as joint stability and efficient breathing can play an important role in overall performance. Reflecting these needs, Frido will showcase two products from its portfolio: Frido Orthotics Sports Knee Cap Support and Frido Nasal Strip Pro. The Knee Cap Support is designed to provide targeted compression and stability during high-impact movement, while the Nasal Strip Pro helps optimize airflow and breathing efficiency during intense physical exertion. Together, these solutions are designed to help participants train, compete and recover with greater confidence and comfort.  Speaking on the association, Ganesh Sonawane, Co-Founder and CEO, Frido , said, “The way consumers approach fitness and wellbeing is evolving rapidly. There is a growing focus on movement quality, recovery and long-term physical health, alongside performance. HYROX has cultivated a community that reflects this shift, making it a natural platform for us to engage with. This partnership aligns with our vision of creating products that help people move more comfortably and confidently, whether they are preparing for competition or navigating everyday life.”  Deepak Raj, Country Head, HYROX India, said, “India is fast becoming one of the most exciting markets for HYROX , with a rapidly growing community of athletes eager to test themselves against a single global standard. We are delighted to welcome Frido as our Knee Cap Partner in Delhi and Nasal Strip Partner in Mumbai , giving participants hands-on access to products built around movement and comfort as they take on the challenge. Partners who share our commitment to performance and wellbeing make the HYROX experience stronger, and we look forward to building this journey together.”  The initiative enables Frido to connect with India's growing community of runners, athletes and fitness enthusiasts while driving greater awareness around the role of movement, recovery and performance-focused solutions in an active lifestyle. Across both events, the brand will engage with participants and spectators, offering firsthand experiences of products designed to enhance endurance, comfort and overall physical performance.","url":"https://businessnewsthisweek.com/business/frido-joins-masters-union-hyrox-delhi-and-mumbai-as-an-official-partner/"},{"date":"2026-06-03","title":"Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru Strengthens its Experiential Retail Portfolio with Sorele, Kameleo and Frido","content":"retail destinations with the addition of emerging D2C and innovation-driven brands Sorele, Kameleo, and Frido.  The latest additions reflect a larger shift in consumer preferences, as shoppers increasingly seek brands that combine individuality, comfort, wellness, and experience-driven retail. As digitally native brands continue expanding into offline spaces, Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru is evolving its retail mix to offer immersive and community-driven shopping experiences tailored to Bengaluru's young, aspirational, and fast-growing consumer base.  Among the newest additions is Sorele, a contemporary fashion jewellery brand known for its minimalist yet modern and versatile collections, crafted with 18K gold plating and lab-grown Moissanite diamonds. Catering to Gen Z, working professionals, and urban families, the brand offers conscious luxury designed to transition seamlessly from workwear to occasion wear.  Enhancing the mall's fashion portfolio is Kameleo, a customised fashion footwear brand focused on creativity and self-expression. Kameleo allows shoppers to personalise footwear by mixing and matching soles and straps across collections such as Candy, Poppi, and Twin, combining vibrant aesthetics with lightweight, all-day comfort for younger consumers seeking personalised fashion experiences.  The launch of Sorele and Kameleo at Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru also marks the brands' first-ever store within a mall format, reflecting a broader shift from high-street retail to destination-led experiential spaces.  Further strengthening the mall's lifestyle and wellness offerings, Frido brings its ergonomics and comfort-led product range focused on posture support, mobility, and everyday wellness. As health-conscious living and functional lifestyle products gain traction among urban consumers, brands like Frido offering strongly aligns with the needs of today's consumers, particularly young tech professionals within the Bhartiya Center of Information Technology ( a tech park within the Bhartiya City ecosystem), alongside families and wellness-conscious shoppers seeking comfort-driven innovations in their daily lives.  The addition of brands such as Sorele, Kameleo, and Frido highlights the growing momentum of digitally native and experiential brands expanding beyond online-first models to build stronger consumer engagement through physical retail environments. Increasingly, consumers want to physically experience and interact with the D2C brands they discover online, and Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru is enabling that transition by bringing these brands closer to customers within an integrated lifestyle destination.  As North Bengaluru rapidly evolves into one of the city's most dynamic residential and commercial growth corridors, Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru continues to build a future-ready retail ecosystem that seamlessly integrates fashion, lifestyle, wellness, dining, and entertainment experiences under one destination. With over 5,000 families moving into North Bengaluru every month, the region is fast emerging as one of Bengaluru's most high-growth real estate markets.  “At Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru, we are seeing a strong shift in how digitally native brands approach offline retail. Today's consumers discover brands online, but they increasingly want immersive physical experiences before making purchase decisions. Brands like Sorele and Kameleo choosing Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru for their first mall stores reflects the strength of our ecosystem and the kind of consumer community we cater to, from young residents and working professionals to families and aspirational shoppers across North Bengaluru. With additions like Frido, we are also strengthening categories centred around wellness, comfort, and lifestyle innovation, which are becoming increasingly relevant for modern urban consumers ,” said Jermina Menon, Brand \u0026 Marketing Strategist, Bhartiya Urban.  With an expanding mix of fashion, lifestyle, wellness, dining, and entertainment offerings, Bhartiya Mall of Bengaluru remains committed to delivering curated retail experiences aligned with the aspirations of Bengaluru's next-generation consumers.","url":"https://businessnewsthisweek.com/business/bhartiya-mall-of-bengaluru-strengthens-its-experiential-retail-portfolio-with-sorele-kameleo-and-frido/"}],"numResults":27},"2":{"investments":[],"totalNumResults":0},"3":{"acquisitions":[],"hasMeaningful